menu "Azure IoT DPS Configuration"

    config AZURE_DPS_ID_SCOPE
        string "DPS ID Scope"
        default "CHANGE_ME_ID_SCOPE"
        help
            From the DPS instance's Overview page in the Azure Portal
            (watgrid-dps -> Overview -> ID Scope).

    config AZURE_DPS_REGISTRATION_ID
        string "DPS Registration ID"
        default "esp32-winegrid"
        help
            Must match the Registration ID configured on an Individual
            Enrollment in the DPS instance (Settings -> Manage enrollments) -
            or, in Group Enrollment mode, is simply this device's chosen
            unique identity within the group (any string, not pre-registered
            anywhere in advance).

    config AZURE_DPS_USE_GROUP_ENROLLMENT
        bool "Use Group Enrollment (derive per-device key from a shared group key)"
        default n
        help
            Off (default): AZURE_DPS_SYMMETRIC_KEY below is used directly as
            this device's own key, matching an Individual Enrollment.
            On: AZURE_DPS_SYMMETRIC_KEY is instead treated as the *group's*
            key (from a Group Enrollment), and this device derives its own
            key locally as HMAC-SHA256(groupKey, AZURE_DPS_REGISTRATION_ID) -
            the same derivation Azure performs server-side to verify it,
            without ever needing a per-device credential provisioned in
            advance. Lets many devices of the same model share one secret,
            each proving a distinct identity.

    config AZURE_DPS_SYMMETRIC_KEY
        string "DPS Symmetric Key (base64) - individual device key, or group key if AZURE_DPS_USE_GROUP_ENROLLMENT is on"
        default "CHANGE_ME_PRIMARY_KEY"
        help
            Primary Key shown on the Individual/Group Enrollment after
            creating it. Used locally to sign SAS tokens (HMAC-SHA256) -
            never sent over the network as-is. Treat as a secret: only ever
            stored in sdkconfig (gitignored), never hardcoded in source.

endmenu